    "notes": [
      "ANACHRONISTIC RELOCATION OF A REAL MARRIAGE (deep-chain audit, 2026-07-03): 'Sir Guy DE LA Spine' (here b.1518) appears to be the real Sir Guy de Spineto of Coughton — whose daughter/coheir Eleanor de Spineto married Sir John Throckmorton, Under-Treasurer of England (d. 1445) — relocated roughly 130-150 years too late and given a garbled surname ('de la Spine'). No Warwickshire/Bedfordshire visitation or peerage source supports a distinct 16th-century Guy/Eleanor 'De La Spine' couple at these dates; treat this generation of the Throckmorton/'De La Spine'/'Bosum'/'Olney' thread as unreliable, though the underlying surnames (Throckmorton, Besford, Olney, Burgoyne) are genuine. — soc.genealogy.medieval Throckmorton pedigree thread; Cracroft's Peerage: Throckmorton of Coughton."
    ]
